        ":question/problem": "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨-\\sqrt{3},0,-2⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨-\\sqrt{3},10,-10⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-\\sqrt{3},0,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\sqrt{3},10,-10⟩ \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{3})\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3})+0\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =3+0+20 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
