        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-317302",
        ":question/problem": "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{7})+(-2)(3)+(5)(-1) \\\\  & =7-6-5 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
